{"name":"Pylon","hex":"#9fbadf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pylon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gateway to the inner part of an Ancient Egyptian temple.","A tower-like structure, usually one of a series, used to support high-voltage electricity cables."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pylon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pylon (architecture)","blocks":[{"text":"In ancient Egyptian architecture, a pylon is a monumental gate of an Egyptian temple. The English word \"pylon\" comes from the Greek term πύλη 'gate'. The Egyptian pylon consists of two pyramidal towers, each tapered and surmounted by a cornice, joined by a less elevated section enclosing the entrance between them. The gate was generally about half the height of the towers. Contemporary paintings of pylons show them with long poles flying banners."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Insel_Philae.JPG/330px-Insel_Philae.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pylon_(architecture)"},{"title":"Tower","blocks":[{"text":"A tower is a tall structure, taller than it is wide, often by a significant factor. Towers are distinguished from masts by their lack of guy-wires and are therefore, along with tall buildings, self-supporting structures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Tokyo_Sky_Tree_2012.JPG/330px-Tokyo_Sky_Tree_2012.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower"},{"title":"Pylon (Beabadoobee album)","blocks":[{"text":"Pylon is the fourth studio album by Filipino-English singer and songwriter Beabadoobee. It was released by English independent label Dirty Hit on 18 September 2026. Its first single, \"Sun Has Set\", was released on the album's announcement date. It was followed by its second single, \"Switchblade\", released on 14 July, and a third single, \"Memories\", on 20 August."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/be/Pylon_%28Beabadoobee_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pylon_(Beabadoobee_album)"},{"title":"Pylon (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Pylon was an American new wave/post-punk band from Athens, Georgia, United States, who were active from 1979 to 1983, 1989 to 1991, and 2004 to 2009. The band consisted of singer Vanessa Briscoe Hay, guitarist Randall Bewley, bassist Michael Lachowski, and drummer Curtis Crowe. They released three studio albums and a number of singles from 1979 to 1990, as well as a live double album in 2016."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Pylon_at_AthFest_2005.jpg/330px-Pylon_at_AthFest_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pylon_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Pylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG/500px-Pylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Pylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG/1280px-Pylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Pylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG/500px-Pylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Luxor Temple","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APylons_and_obelisk_Luxor_temple.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Sydney_harbour_bridge_new_south_wales.jpg/500px-Sydney_harbour_bridge_new_south_wales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu